#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:1
msgid "Release 2.3 (2019-09-04)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:3
msgid ""
"This is primarily a bug fix release. However, it makes some incompatible "
"changes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:6
msgid ""
"Nix now uses BSD file locks instead of POSIX file locks. Because of this, "
"you should not use Nix 2.3 and previous releases at the same time on a Nix "
"store."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:10
msgid "It also has the following changes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:12
msgid ""
"`builtins.fetchGit`'s `ref` argument now allows specifying an absolute "
"remote ref. Nix will automatically prefix `ref` with `refs/heads` only if "
"`ref` doesn't already begin with `refs/`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:16
msgid ""
"The installer now enables sandboxing by default on Linux when the system has "
"the necessary kernel support."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:19
msgid "The `max-jobs` setting now defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:21
msgid "New builtin functions: `builtins.isPath`, `builtins.hashFile`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:23
msgid ""
"The `nix` command has a new `--print-build-logs` (`-L`) flag to print build "
"log output to stderr, rather than showing the last log line in the progress "
"bar. To distinguish between concurrent builds, log lines are prefixed by the "
"name of the package."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:28
msgid ""
"Builds are now executed in a pseudo-terminal, and the `TERM` environment "
"variable is set to `xterm-256color`. This allows many programs (e.g. `gcc`, "
"`clang`, `cmake`) to print colorized log output."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:33
msgid ""
"Add `--no-net` convenience flag. This flag disables substituters; sets the "
"`tarball-ttl` setting to infinity (ensuring that any previously downloaded "
"files are considered current); and disables retrying downloads and sets the "
"connection timeout to the minimum. This flag is enabled automatically if "
"there are no configured non-loopback network interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:40
msgid ""
"Add a `post-build-hook` setting to run a program after a build has succeeded."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.3.md:43
msgid ""
"Add a `trace-function-calls` setting to log the duration of Nix function "
"calls to stderr."
msgstr ""
